---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: HEYwire pricing
description: Straight pricing for low-voltage work. Per-drop pricing, no surprise line items, and a number fixed for 30 days.
---
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
    <h1 class="h1">Straight pricing.<br>Straight runs.</h1>
    <p class="lede">The number you see is the number you pay. Here is how it is built, so nothing on the invoice is a surprise.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container grid grid--3">
    <div class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">1 · Clear pricing</p>
      <p class="price">Starting at $279<a class="fn-ref" href="#travel-note" aria-label="Taxes and travel additional">**</a></p>
      <p class="card__text">CAT6, pulled, terminated, tested, and labeled. The base price covers a standard run in a standard building.</p>
      <p class="card__fine" id="travel-note">** Taxes and travel additional.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">2 · Conditionals</p>
      <p class="price">Shown up front</p>
      <p class="card__text">Plenum jacket, long runs, hard-lid ceilings, after-hours windows, and lift work are called out in the estimate before you confirm.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">3 · Valid for 30 days</p>
      <p class="price">No change orders<span class="price__unit">without your OK</span></p>
      <p class="card__text">If the site is not what the quote assumed, the crew stops and shows you the difference before doing the work.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="h2">What is always included</h2>
    <ul class="proof proof--2col">
      <li class="proof__item"><span class="proof__check">{% include "svg/icon-check.svg" %}</span><span>Materials: cable, jacks, faceplates, patch panel ports, and patch cords.</span></li>
      <li class="proof__item"><span class="proof__check">{% include "svg/icon-check.svg" %}</span><span>Certification to category spec, with results sent to you.</span></li>
      <li class="proof__item"><span class="proof__check">{% include "svg/icon-check.svg" %}</span><span>Labels at both ends that match the test report.</span></li>
      <li class="proof__item"><span class="proof__check">{% include "svg/icon-check.svg" %}</span><span>Cleanup, ceiling tiles back, debris removed.</span></li>
      <li class="proof__item"><span class="proof__check">{% include "svg/icon-check.svg" %}</span><span>A 365-day workmanship warranty on every run.<a class="fn-ref" href="#warranty-note" aria-label="Warranty terms">*</a></span></li>
      <li class="proof__item"><span class="proof__check">{% include "svg/icon-check.svg" %}</span><span>Nights, weekends, and turnover windows at the rate shown in the quote.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="h3 addons__title">Optional add-ons</h3>
    <ul class="proof proof--2col">
      <li class="proof__item"><span class="proof__check proof__check--plus">+</span><span><strong>As-built drawings.</strong> Marked-up floor plans showing every run, jack, and patch panel port. Priced per floor and shown on the quote before you confirm.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="footnote" id="warranty-note">* Warranty covers our workmanship for 365 days from completion. Excludes damage done by others, such as cables severed or damaged after we leave, and weather, water, corrosion, or similar environmental damage.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="h2">What changes the price</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="table">
        <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>What it means</th><th>How it shows up</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Jacket rating</td><td>Plenum where the code requires it, riser elsewhere</td><td>Fixed add per drop</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Run length</td><td>Unusually long runs from the closet take more cable and more time</td><td>Fixed add per drop</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ceiling type</td><td>Drop tile is standard; hard lid or open deck takes longer</td><td>Fixed add per drop</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Access</td><td>High ceilings or hard-to-reach spaces that call for a lift or scaffold</td><td>Fixed add per day</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Window</td><td>Nights, weekends, or a turnover deadline</td><td>Fixed add per visit</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Volume</td><td>More drops in one visit cost less each</td><td>Shown as a lower per-drop price</td></tr>
          <tr><td>As-built drawings</td><td>Optional. Marked-up plans of every run, jack, and port</td><td>Add-on, priced per floor</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">Fiber, AV, cameras, and guest room work are priced the same way, with their own base and adjustments. Every line is on the quote before you confirm.</p>
  </div>
</section>

